OL,3,ANew photos are 'essential evidence' of
OL,4,Apossible SAS war crimes, inquiry told
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn inquiry into UK special forces
OL,7,Foperations in Afghanistan has released
OL,8,Fphotos described as "essential
OL,9,Fevidence", showing soldiers could have
OL,10,Fexecuted unarmed people lying asleep.
OL,12,FFor the first time, the inquiry has
OL,13,Fmade public photos taken of the
OL,14,Fdeceased, across two SAS operations,
OL,15,Fthat show multiple individuals lying in
OL,16,Fbed with shots to the head.
OL,18,FThe inquiry's lead barrister, Oliver
OL,19,FGlasgow KC, said the photos may be
OL,20,Fevidence of possible war crimes and
OL,21,Fworthy of expert interrogation.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
